        }
      ],
      "words": 39
    },
    {
      "block": "原句3",
      "no": 3,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "It was my turn for a shot. I let it burn. “I called the ghost cops on François.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 5992
        }
      ],
      "words": 18
    },
    {
      "block": "原句4",
      "no": 4,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“People fuck up,” Julie said. “That’s inevitable. What did you do after that?”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 6144
        }
      ],
      "words": 13
    },
    {
      "block": "原句5",
      "no": 5,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“You mean the ghost cops have a fucking ghost jail?” There was a fire behind her eyes now",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 6434
        }
      ],
      "words": 18
    },
    {
      "block": "原句6",
      "no": 6,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“I don’t think these guys really see them, because then they’d have to admit it. I think they’re doing what they’re doin",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 6785
        }
      ],
      "words": 27
    },
    {
      "block": "原句7",
      "no": 7,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“To Mary Ellen, then.” We clinked glasses and she threw hers back",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 7478
        }
      ],
      "words": 12
    },
    {
      "block": "原句8",
      "no": 8,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“Was she see-through?”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 7619
        },
        {
          "text": "“It’s like you can see them, but somehow you also know they aren’t really there. It’s kinda like a trick of the light.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 7673
        }
      ],
      "words": 27
    },
    {
      "block": "原句9",
      "no": 9,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Plus, I never got what my mother used to say when I was little out of my head: Don’t trust anyone who says the first one",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 3867
        }
      ],
      "words": 27
    },
    {
      "block": "原句10",
      "no": 10,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“It’s a philosophical issue, you know? Who is a city really for?”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 4442
        }
      ],
      "words": 12
    },
    {
      "block": "原句11",
      "no": 11,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Who needs Robert Moses,” she started yelling, “when you got planned shrinkage! Let the subways go to shit, the schools, ",
          "ok": true,
